      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey i'm stuck on this macro for our monthly recon report. it works fine most of the time but lately it keeps crashing on this line:\n\nSub MonthlyRecon()\n    Dim ws As Worksheet\n    Set ws = ThisWorkbook.Sheets(\"Reconciliation_Final\")\n    ws.Range(\"A1:Z100\").ClearContents\n    ws.Range(\"B2\").Value = \"Report Run Date: \" & Date\n    ' ... rest of code\nEnd Sub\n\ni keep getting \"Run-time error '1004': Application-defined or object-defined error\". can u help me figure out why it keeps happening?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A \"Run-time error '1004'\" on a line like that, especially when it's usually fine, often points to a hidden issue with the worksheet or the range itself. It's usually not the code structure, but something external, like a protected sheet or a corrupted range reference. Try checking if the \"Reconciliation\\_Final\" sheet is protected, as that can cause the `.ClearContents` command to fail. If it is protected, you'll need to unprotect it before running the macro, or add code to unprotect/reprotect it.",
